    {
      "id": "S01",
      "finding": "Protected checkpoint reconstruction is explicit: strict official PV state, original G state delta, then the 4506 distribution-refiner delta; the newly installed R has a zero output projection. The probe freezes all parameters, uses eval mode, and asserts the semantic query before/after R is exactly equal on every observed forward.",
      "evidence": [
        "readback_model_factory.py:15-75",
        "pvground_boundary_evidence_readback.py:27-29",
        "run_mask_geometry_probe.py:116-138,235-239"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "S02",
      "finding": "The actual detection-aligned Joint3DDataset is imported before model modules. Its local source identity matches the input appearance manifest and the completed fit imports record. Model losses/main_utils/prepare_data and the source-preview PVGround identities also match the prior actual import receipt; losses.py is the unchanged native criterion identified by the selected source port.",
      "evidence": [
        "run_mask_geometry_probe.py:47-72,94-114",
        "complete/quality/imports.json",
        "joint_det_dataset.py:1260-1275"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "S03",
      "finding": "The generated fit dataset, preparation, RNG reset and seeded B8/2-worker shuffled loader derive from the executed runner. The probe enables point and detected-box augmentation, prepares train voxels, retains the first eight batches, and compares each batch row list with the first eight completed fit log records. The local log has 8 batches of 8 distinct rows (64 unique rows); actual new-run equality remains a runtime assertion.",
      "evidence": [
        "prepare_probe.py:12-26",
        "run_mask_geometry_probe.py:140-195,214-231,347-351",
        "run_final_quality_fit.py:237-254,423-449"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "S04",
      "finding": "The hook observes the real native matcher calls, without substituting targets. Native prefix order is proposal,last,0head..4head; captured[1] is the actual final layer. The probe verifies those boxes and valid training-GT boxes exactly, then maps compressed target indices through valid[targets] back to original GT slots.",
      "evidence": [
        "models/losses.py:808-846,849-917",
        "run_mask_geometry_probe.py:232-245,263-276",
        "joint_det_dataset.py:1086-1119"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "S05",
      "finding": "Detached final Box-leaf gradients replay the native loss_boxes routine with the native matched count and coefficients (10*L1+2*GIoU)/7. Detached boundary-logit gradients replay distribution_loss/7 with the same actual final indices and actual valid GT labels. These losses only index matched queries; the probe explicitly checks finite gradients and exact zero gradient at unmatched outputs.",
      "evidence": [
        "models/losses.py:518-559,831-835,947-955",
        "pvground_boundary_box_refiner.py:40-65",
        "run_mask_geometry_probe.py:247-276"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "S06",
      "finding": "The fused Mask is sigmoid(alpha*text_logit+(1-alpha)*query_logit)>0.5, matching the native evaluator. Per-superpoint total and root-positive member counts produce the point-weighted intersection and union for all 256 candidates; this is not a mean of superpoint IoUs. The selected query is additionally checked against explicit point expansion, and the native signed root bbs score is used for selection.",
      "evidence": [
        "src/grounding_evaluator.py:250-286,594-650",
        "native_root_bbs.py:4-9",
        "run_mask_geometry_probe.py:259-296"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "S07",
      "finding": "The generated executable contains no optimizer construction, optimizer step, model backward or checkpoint-save call. Model forward and full native criterion execute under no_grad, and the only two autograd.grad calls target detached output leaves. The terminal receipt is written only after 64 rows, absent model parameter gradients and exact before/after state_dict equality are asserted.",
      "evidence": [
        "run_mask_geometry_probe.py:235-258,349-365",
        "prepare_probe.py:18-28"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "S08",
